# Activity log

After a task that changes the project or produces a durable result, append one entry to `docs/activity_log.md` before you finish.

Log code, configuration, documentation, and investigation that leaves files or findings behind. Unpacking an artifact or finishing an analysis step counts. A chat reply that changes nothing does not.

Do not add an entry when the only changes are in `docs/activity_log.md`, `docs/pemahaman.md`, Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/`), or skills (`SKILL.md`, including `.cursor/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`). If the task also changes project code, artifacts, or findings, still log that work.

## Append only

The file only grows. Existing entries are a permanent record.

- Add one new entry per task, not per file.
- Never edit, delete, reorder, or redate an existing entry.
- A later task does not revise an earlier entry, including to fix a mistake. Write the correction as a new entry and leave the old one unchanged.
- Insert the new entry at the top, directly under `# Activity Log`.
- Write the entry in Indonesian.
- Put lasting facts in `docs/pemahaman.md` as a new timestamped record. Repeat a fact here only when it is part of what that task found.

## Format

The heading timestamp is the recording time in Western Indonesian Time (WIB, UTC+7), 24-hour clock, minute precision. Set it once, when the entry is written. Do not backdate it, and do not change it later.

Clock times recovered for entries written before this format existed are final. Do not change them again. If a future entry has a date and no clock time, leave it; do not invent a time.

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm WIB — Judul singkat

### Tujuan
Apa yang dikerjakan dan mengapa.

### Perubahan
- `path/file`: apa yang ditambah, dihapus, atau diubah.

### Status
Selesai, sebagian, atau diblokir. Sebutkan sisa kerja jika ada.
```

Add `### Temuan` only when the task discovered something worth keeping in the history.

When an entry names a class, method, field, or other symbol from reverse-engineered code, follow `.cursor/rules/docs-sumber-kode.mdc`: link the workspace file and include a short snippet in the new entry. A name alone is not enough. Do not edit an older entry to add that citation.
